{"id":"leetcode-1491","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Average Salary Excluding the Minimum and Maximum Salary","summary":"Given an array of distinct integers representing employee salaries, calculate the average salary excluding the highest and lowest values.","statement":"Given an array of distinct integers representing employee salaries, calculate the average salary excluding the highest and lowest values. Results within 0.00001 of the true average are acceptable.","constraints":["At least three distinct salaries are provided.","Return the average after excluding one minimum and one maximum."],"topics":["arrays","math"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"average_middle_salary","parameters":[{"name":"salary","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"float","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def average_middle_salary(salary: list[int]) -> float:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def average_middle_salary(salary):\n return (sum(salary)-min(salary)-max(salary))/(len(salary)-2)\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def average_middle_salary(salary):\n return (sum(salary)+min(salary)-max(salary))/(len(salary)-2)\n","def average_middle_salary(salary):\n return (sum(salary)-min(salary)-max(salary))/(len(salary))\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Subtract the unique minimum and maximum from the total.","The remaining count is len-2.","Divide remaining sum by remaining count.","Distinctness ensures exactly the intended two entries are removed."],"editorial":"Distinctness ensures exactly the intended two entries are removed.","tests":[{"id":"lc-1491-1","arguments":[[4000,3000,1000,2000]],"expected